# Unconstrained mutation rejects an incompatible base

Verifies an unconstrained `int[]` still enforces its base-type contract and
rejects replacing an integer element with a string.

>>> source
let values: int[] = [1]
values[0] = "hello"

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: string literals are not supported by type `int64` at Span { start: 36, end: 43 }

<<< exit
1
